# Styling: Tailwind-first (NativeWind)

All visual styling goes through NativeWind `className`. Reach for
`StyleSheet` / inline `style` only when Tailwind literally cannot express
the property (animated values, dynamic numeric tokens from `theme.ts`,
shadow objects, platform-specific SDK props).

## Do

- Use `className="..."` on `View`, `Pressable`, `ScrollView`, `ThemedText`,
  etc.
- Express layout, spacing, typography, radius, and color utilities with
  Tailwind classes first.
- Pull dynamic values from `@/constants/theme` and pass them via `style`
  only when needed (e.g. animated gradients, computed shadows).

```tsx
// Good
<View className="flex-row items-center gap-3 rounded-2xl bg-white/5 px-4 py-3">
  <ThemedText className="text-[15px] font-semibold">Hello</ThemedText>
</View>

// Good — mixing className with a dynamic token only for what Tailwind can't
<View
  className="rounded-2xl px-4 py-3"
  style={{ backgroundColor: theme.backgroundElement, ...Shadows.userBubble }}
/>
```

## Do not

- Do not author new `StyleSheet.create({...})` blocks for what Tailwind can
  express (`padding`, `margin`, `flex*`, colors, typography, radii).
- Do not hardcode hex colors in `style`; import `Brand`, `Gradients`, or
  `Colors` from `@/constants/theme`.
- Do not add CSS modules (`.module.css`) or `styled-components` — neither
  is set up for this app.
- Do not mix `className` and a duplicate `style` prop for the same property.

```tsx
// Bad — Tailwind covers all of this
const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  row: { flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', padding: 12 },
});
<View style={styles.row} />

// Good
<View className="flex-row items-center p-3" />
```

## Tokens

- Colors/spacing tokens that Tailwind can't read are in
  `src/constants/theme.ts` (`Brand`, `Gradients`, `Shadows`, `Spacing`,
  `BottomTabInset`, `MaxContentWidth`). Use them via `style={...}` when a
  numeric/object is required.
- Theme-aware text/surface colors come from `useTheme()` — apply via
  `style={{ color: theme.text }}` since they're runtime values.
